<title>UK: Courtaulds denies Singapore plant report.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds denies Singapore plant report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemicals group Courtaulds Plc on Monday denied a report in The Times that it was close to finalising plans to build a new plant in Singapore for production its Tencel fibre.</p>
<p>&quot;The report is erroneous,&quot; a Courtaulds spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The position has not been changed: we are looking into a number of options in Asia and Singapore is one of them and we will make an announcement later this year,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
